{"text": "BRADLEY L. COMPTON\ncompton4mayor@gmail.com\n3724 NE 15\" Street\n\nMiami, Florida 33033\n305.219.6594\n\nEDUCATION\nUniversity of Miami, Rosenstiel School of Marine and Atmospheric Sciences, Virginia Key,\nFlorida\nMaster of Arts, Marine Affairs and Policy, December 2004\nEmphasis on fisheries management and offshore aquaculture\nUniversity of Miami School of Law, Coral Gables, Florida\nJuris Doctor, June 2003\nEmphasis on business law and marine environmental law\nActivities: | Phi Delta Phi, Legal Honor Society, 2001 \u2014 Present\nUniversity of Miami School of Law Ambassador, 2000-2003\nOklahoma State University, Stillwater, Oklahoma\nBachelor of Science, General Business, May 2000\nEmphasis on Economics, Finance, and Management\nHonors: Golden Key National Honor Society, 1999 \u2014 Present\nActivities: | Zeta Beta Tau, Founding Member, 1998 \u2014 Present\nVice President, 1999 \u2014 2000\nAlpha Kappa Psi, 1999 \u2014 Present\nProfessional Chair, 1999 \u2014 2000\n\nEXPERIENCE\nCRB Geological & Environmental Services, Inc., Coral Gables, Florida\nProject Manager, January 2005 \u2014 Present\nWorked in a team environment to market CRB\u2019s environmental services and managed\nclient relationships. Clearly communicated with users, property owners, and regulatory\nagency personnel and efficiently reviewed regulatory files and historical sources to\nconduct environmental site assessments to facilitate property transactions, development,\nand lending activities at over 200 properties. Effectively conducted more than 35 site\nassessments and over 20 active remediation projects, including using innovative\ntechnologies, in multiple states to achieve regulatory closure on more than 15 properties.\nManaged, conducted, and supervised hundreds asbestos projects including asbestos\nsurveys, abatement projects, air clearance sampling and analysis, and management\nplans. These projects required coordinating with and overseeing of field personnel and\nsubcontractors; managing a team of asbestos abatement contractors and workers,\nenvironmental scientists, geologists, hydrologists, and engineers; interfacing with\nregulatory agencies; and preparing reports of asbestos surveys, asbestos abatements,\nenvironmental assessment activities, and recommendations.\nEnvironment Matters, Inc., Tampa, Florida\nOffshore Aquaculture Legislative Assistant, May 2004 \u2014 December 2004\nInteracted with state agencies and non-governmental agencies to establish\ncomprehensive offshore aquaculture regulations and prepared offshore aquaculture\neducational materials to educate stakeholders, regulators and the general public.",
